  "body": "Elevated in one of Red Beach's most tightly held pockets, 6 Durness Place offers a rare combination of spectacular panoramic coastal views, effortless single-level living and exciting future potential on a freehold site.\r\n\r\nTop features you'll love:\r\n\r\n- Outstanding coastal views across the Hibiscus Coast to Great Barrier Island and top of the Coromandel\r\n- Three double bedrooms and two modernised bathrooms\r\n- Generous open-plan living designed to embrace the outlook\r\n- Elevated, private position in a quiet cul-de-sac\r\n- Beautifully manicured gardens and a fully fenced section\r\n- Generous, level off-street parking at the front of the property; bring the boat or caravan\r\n- Comfortable as it stands, with scope to modernise to to suit your needs\r\n- Easy access to Red Beach via the shortcut at the end of Durness Place\r\n\r\nIt's the lifestyle here that's hard to beat. Morning swims at the beach, weekend breakfast at the Red Beach Surf Club, and the convenience of having so much of the Coast's best within easy reach. Yet once you step inside, there's a remarkable sense of privacy, with beautifully established gardens creating inviting spaces to relax and entertain.\r\n\r\nFor the current owners, it's the ever-changing coastal panorama they've loved most. From watching every changing skies across the Coast to spotting orcas in the bay, the outlook is something special in every season.\r\n\r\nThe home itself offers comfortable, easy living, with the bathrooms already modernised and plenty of opportunity for future owners to add their own style. Whether you choose to enjoy it just as it is or explore the potential, this is a position worth investing in.\r\n\r\nOpportunities to secure a freehold property with views like these, in such a tightly held Red Beach location, are few and far between.  Your early viewing is recommended at open homes or private viewing.",
